  "raw": {
    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/assistant-associate-professor-counseling-houston-texas-united-states": {
      "title": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Counseling",
      "description": "Assistant/Associate Professor, Counseling - Houston, Texas, United States Assistant/Associate Professor, Counseling - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Assistant/Associate Professor, Counseling 497070 Full-Time Leadership & Policy Analysis Description: The College of Education at the University of Houston–Clear Lake invites applications for a 9-month, full-time tenure-track position at the Assistant/Associate Professor rank. The successful candidate will meet requirements to serve as a Core Faculty member as outlined in the 2024 CACREP Standards in our CACREP-accredited Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program. Responsibilities include teaching graduate courses in the CMHC program, collaborating with program faculty and community stakeholders to revise and refine program curriculum as needed, building and sustaining partnerships with community mental health agencies and schools, providing supervision and clinical oversight for students in internships, contributing to program governance and accreditation efforts, sustaining robust research and dissemination activities, and engaging in service to the school, college, university, community, and the profession. Duties: Provide teaching and supervision across the clinical mental health curriculum, supporting program and student needs. Contribute actively to curriculum design and program enhancement, ensuring alignment with a broad representation of current research, professional standards, accreditation requirements, and emerging trends in counselor education and practice. Conduct and publish high-quality research in reputable academic journals and present findings at conferences, contributing to the field's knowledge base. Engage in service activities within the program, department, college, university, professional organizations, and leadership opportunities over time. Qualifications Required: Doctoral degree in Counselor Education and Supervision, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program. Currently licensed as an LPC or LPC-S, or eligible to obtain Texas LPC licensure. Knowledge and understanding of disciplinary subject matter at a level adequate for graduate-level instruction; written and oral communication skills sufficient to conduct effective teaching and research activities; ability to interact with students, staff, and faculty in a professional, collegial, and collaborative manner. Evidence or, or potential to develop, a sustained scholarly agenda resulting in peer-reviewed publications, presentations, and external funding. Preferred: Doctoral degree in Counselor Education and Supervision from a CACREP-accredited program. Interest in interdisciplinary collaborations, research, and academic innovation across the college's academic departments and university. Experience teaching and supervising graduate counseling students in a CACREP-accredited program. Required Attachments by Candidate: 1) Curriculum Vitae, 2) a Letter of Application that addresses the required and preferred qualifications and highlights teaching philosophy and experience, 3) unofficial graduate transcripts, and 4) three letters of reference. Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Official transcripts will be required for the finalists who are invited for on-campus interviews and a background check is required. Position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu . All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Recommended postings Nurse Practitioner 497197 Student Affairs-Health, Wellness & Comm Full-Time Division of Student Affairs Medical Assistant 497198 Student Affairs-Health, Wellness & Comm Full-Time Division of Student Affairs Administrative Assistant II 497104 Academic Affairs-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education Business Operations Assistant 497069 VP, Admin & Finance-Business Operations Full-Time Division of Administration and Finance Application Systems Analyst 497079 Strat Enrollment Mgmt-VP of SEM PH - LVL 4 Full-Time Division of Strategic Enrollment Management Assistant/Associate Professor, Counseling 497070 Academic Affairs-College of Edu Full-Time College of Education - Transformative Leadership, Counseling, & Innovation Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Profile link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.uh.edu/jobs/visiting-assistant-professor-counseling-houston-texas-united-states-5517d03b-76c0-4908-bc1b-46a9e2afd74d": {
      "title": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling",
      "description": "Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling - Houston, Texas, United States Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling - Houston, Texas, United States Kiosk mode Visiting Assistant Professor, Counseling 497050 Full-Time Leadership & Policy Analysis Department: Transformative Leadership, Counseling, & Innovation Salary: Commensurate with Experience/Education Description: The Department of Transformative Leadership, Counseling, and Innovation at the University of Houston-Clear Lake (UHCL) invites applications for the position of Visiting Assistant Professor in its CACREP-accredited Clinical Mental Health Counseling (CMHC) program. The successful candidate will contribute to the development and growth of the counseling program, teach graduate counseling courses, and provide service to the program, university, and profession. This position will be for Spring 2027 and may be renewed based on program need. The Visiting Assistant Professor may apply for a tenure-track position if one is advertised and the required qualifications are met. Applications are accepted only through the UHCL Job Opportunities website. To apply, please complete the online application and attach a letter of interest, curriculum vitae, statements of research and teaching interests, and evidence of teaching excellence. Review of completed applications will begin immediately and continue until the position is filled, with priority given to applications received by October 15, 2026. Interviews will take place online, and a teaching demonstration will be part of the final interview process. Duties: Teach graduate courses across the counseling curriculum, with particular emphasis on clinical mental health counseling Contribute to curriculum development and accreditation data collection and documentation Provide clinical supervision to practicum and internship students Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with community agencies and clinical partners Maintain an active counselor educator identity through professional engagement, practice, scholarship, service, and advocacy, as appropriate to the faculty role Participate in college activities and serve on program or college committees Participate in program, college, university, and professional service activities Qualifications Required: An earned doctorate in Counselor Education and Supervision, preferably from a CACREP-accredited program Evidence of a counselor and counselor educator identity through sustained professional engagement in at least two of the following areas: counseling-related professional development and renewal; professional service and advocacy; ongoing counseling practice; or research and scholarly activity commensurate with the faculty role Texas LPC licensure or eligibility for Texas LPC licensure Excellent communication skills Preferred: Successful university teaching experience Evidence of or potential for scholarly activity Demonstrated professional or academic service Experience providing clinical mental health counseling Experience teaching clinical mental health counseling students Experience using a learning management system and teaching in online or hybrid formats Experience with CACREP accreditation processes Experience providing clinical supervision to practicum or internship students Required Attachments by Candidate: Curriculum Vitae, Cover Letter/Letter of Application, Teaching Philosophy or Statement, Evidence of Effective Teaching Note: Please combine all supporting documents into one file for attachment to your application. Position is not eligible for H-1B sponsorship. For any questions on this posting, please contact FacultyAffairs@uhcl.edu. All positions at the University of Houston-System are security sensitive and will require a criminal history check. The University of Houston System and its universities are Equal Opportunity Institutions. Everyone is encouraged to apply. Apply now First Name (required) 6e15b929 Last Name (required) 4a6d06e5 